Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:10:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] pinebook-pro: read the SPI flash at 25 MHz instead of 10 MHz

The flash node has spi-max-frequency = <10000000>, so SPL reads the
1.2 MB U-Boot FIT at about 10 MHz on every boot. On this Pinebook Pro,
reads in U-Boot are correct at 9.9, 14.1, 19.8, 24.75 and 33 MHz and
wrong at 49.5 MHz (the controller divides 198 MHz by even numbers).
Use 25 MHz (24.75 MHz real), well below the speed that fails.
CONFIG_SF_DEFAULT_SPEED is set to the same value in the board recipe,
because SPL's spi_flash_probe() passes it and it overrides the DT speed.
---
 arch/arm/dts/rk3399-pinebook-pro-u-boot.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-pinebook-pro-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-pinebook-pro-u-boot.dtsi
index 2e3573f..3802368 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-pinebook-pro-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-pinebook-pro-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@
 };
 
 &spiflash {
+	spi-max-frequency = <25000000>;
 	bootph-all;
 };
 
